{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fvjp2jpv5yly426penfhjhys6wyc7ndl5e7t2bkt4ebsyssq24iq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All verification complete. Final state confirmed green, and `c_src/` sources are untouched (original 09:30 timestamps; only the instructed `build/` dir was added).\n\n## Result: no divergences found in the translation\n\nThe project turned out to be a single-file **executable** (`add_executable(driver src/main.c)`), not a library — 16 lines of C: `print_hex` (static), `driver`, and `main` doing `float x = 0.f; scanf(\"%f\", &x); driver(x); return 0;`. Almost all observable behaviour comes from glibc's `scanf(\"%f\")`/`strtof`, which `src/lib.rs` reimplements from scratch. That's where I concentrated verification.\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (all derived mechanically from the C source):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — C exe exports *zero* defined dynamic symbols (only 7 libc/toolchain imports); global text symbols are `{driver, main}`, `print_hex` is `static`\n- `ERRORS.md` — 25 rows, all checked\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 62 rows, all checked\n\n**Phases B–D:** 75 tests across 4 build configurations (2 feature combos × 2 profiles), all passing:\n\n```\nok  features=<none>  profile=dev      (75 tests)\nok  features=<none>  profile=release  (75 tests)\nok  features=c_main  profile=dev      (75 tests)\nok  features=c_main  profile=release  (75 tests)\n```\n\n`tests/ffi_diff.rs` loads **both** implementations as `.so` via `libloading` and calls the exported `driver` symbol — the Rust side is never called directly.\n\n**Beyond the suite**, `tools/` fuzzers found zero divergences over ~**700 000** inputs, including *exhaustive* coverage of all strings up to length 3 (17-char alphabet), length 4 (11-char), and length 5 (7-char), plus exact dyadic midpoints for ties-to-even and targeted sweeps of the `dp>45`/`dp<-50`, 60-bit-accumulator/sticky-bit, and `e_val>127`/`shift>=64` cutoffs.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n\n1. **Only one real bug was found, and it was in my own test**, not the translation: I asserted `\"1.5\\0\"` → `1.0f`; the C correctly yields `1.5f`. Corrected to match the C. Three harness bugs were also fixed (stale/missing cdylib, fd-1 capture racing libtest's parallel progress lines, `not(test)` on the exported `main`) — none were translation issues.\n\n2. **I made a structural change to the crate** you should be aware of: split `src/main.rs` into `lib.rs` + thin `main.rs` with `crate-type = [\"cdylib\",\"rlib\"]` so the `#[no_mangle]` export could be tested through the FFI boundary, and added a `c_main` feature that exports a C-ABI `main` (a real translation of `int main()`, not a stub) purely so the `.so` symbol diff against the C `.so` reaches empty. `default = []`, so `cargo build --release` produces a behaviourally identical binary — re-verified with the full sweep after the refactor.\n\nThe error surface has one inherent limitation worth stating: because `main` discards `scanf`'s return value, *every* rejection surfaces as the same `00000000\\n`. Asserting \"both rejected\" would be vacuous, so Phase C rows 14–21 assert distinct non-zero sentinels instead (e.g. `\"0x1p\"` → `0000803f`, proving glibc backs the dangling `p` out rather than failing)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":877,"cache_read_input_tokens":180206,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":877,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f77dfa2-0d98-4f8d-9ab4-2b55bea5ed0d","uuid":"01282211-fcc9-4a05-ad8c-7fbe68dc0d94","timestamp":"2026-08-18T10:17:26.316Z"}
